From c2d8d5987d5254b7d755bbb03a989ec92c99e2be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tillmann Severin <tillmann.severin@mailbox.org>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 15:17:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/26] net: hix5hd2_gmac: accept the RGMII internal delay
 modes

hix5hd2_set_desc_depth()'s caller configures the MAC interface from
priv->phy_mode, but the switch statement only ever matched
PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RGMII.  A board that describes its link as
"rgmii-id", "rgmii-rxid" or "rgmii-txid" therefore fell through to the
default case, was rejected as "not supported mode" and got configured
for MII at 10 Mbit/s instead of RGMII.

The *-id variants only tell the PHY driver to enable its internal RX
and/or TX delay lines; from the MAC's point of view they are plain
RGMII and need exactly the same configuration.  Let them share the
RGMII case.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hix5hd2_gmac.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hix5hd2_gmac.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hix5hd2_gmac.c
index e3e7f2270560..0665f1cd9da3 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hix5hd2_gmac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/hisilicon/hix5hd2_gmac.c
@@ -292,6 +292,9 @@ static void hix5hd2_config_port(struct net_device *dev, u32 speed, u32 duplex)
 
 	switch (priv->phy_mode) {
 	case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RGMII:
+	case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RGMII_ID:
+	case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RGMII_RXID:
+	case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RGMII_TXID:
 		if (speed == SPEED_1000)
 			val = RGMII_SPEED_1000;
 		else if (speed == SPEED_100)
